  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#start-tags\r\n\r\n> Tags contain a tag name, giving the element's name\\. HTML elements all have names that only use ASCII alphanumerics\\. In the HTML syntax, tag names, even those for foreign elements, may be written with any mix of lower\\- and uppercase letters that, when converted to all\\-lowercase, matches the element's tag name; tag names are case\\-insensitive\\.\r\n\r\nFrom this paragraph we can conclude that for html-tags ASCII alphanumeric is used. But what about custom elements? This paragraph does not say anything about him. Custom element is not the HTML element? I think this paragraph should be supplemented with information. If nothing is worth adding, explain how the custom element is related to or not related to this paragraph.",
